<main id="main" tabindex="-1">
<section id="intro" class="chapter is-active" data-scene="intro" aria-label="Introduction"><div class="chapter__inner">
<h1 class="home-title">Structured data in ordinary Markdown files</h1>
<p>Keep notes, tasks and projects as Markdown files. mdbase syncs them between your devices and serves them to the apps you use, on any device, with the permissions you give each app.</p>
<div class="chapter__actions home-actions"><a class="home-action home-action--primary" href="https://connect.mdbase.dev/signup">Create an account</a><a class="home-action" href="/downloads/">Download the desktop app</a></div>
<p class="v2-status">mdbase is in beta. Keep independent backups of important collections.</p>
</div></section>

<section id="files" class="chapter" data-scene="collection" aria-label="Files"><div class="chapter__inner">
<h2>The same task in an app and on disk</h2>
<p>A collection is a folder of Markdown records. Each record’s frontmatter holds fields that apps can validate and query, and its body stays ordinary prose.</p>
<AppShot name="tasknotes" alt="TaskNotes showing today's tasks. The first is Send the research summary to Rowan, due tomorrow, high priority." />
<pre class="record-example v2-record" aria-label="The task as a file: tasks/research-summary-for-rowan.md"><code><span class="v2-path">tasks/research-summary-for-rowan.md</span>
<span class="fm-rule">---</span>
<span class="fm-key">title:</span> Send the research summary to Rowan
<span class="fm-key">status:</span> open
<span class="fm-key">priority:</span> high
<span class="fm-key">due:</span> 2026-11-10
<span class="fm-rule">---</span>

Include the interview notes from
the field visit.</code></pre>
<p>When you tick the task in TaskNotes, the app sets <code>status: done</code> in this file. Because records are plain files, the folder works with git, backups and any text editor, and it stays yours if you stop using mdbase.</p>
</div></section>

<section id="apps" class="chapter" data-scene="apps" aria-label="Apps"><div class="chapter__inner">
<h2>One collection, many apps</h2>
<p>Apps built on mdbase work on these files directly. Several can open the same collection at once, so nothing is exported from one app to another.</p>
<dl class="v2-apps-list">
<div><dt><a href="https://app.tasknotes.dev/">TaskNotes</a></dt><dd>Tasks, calendars and reminders, on the web, iOS and Android.</dd></div>
<div><dt><a href="/apps/editor/">Editor</a></dt><dd>Any collection: records, frontmatter, links and types.</dd></div>
<div><dt><a href="/apps/reader/">Reader</a></dt><dd>PDFs, EPUBs and web pages, with each highlight kept as a record.</dd></div>
<div><dt><a href="/apps/writer/">Writer</a></dt><dd>Papers and books in Markdown, with citations from Reader.</dd></div>
</dl>
<p><a href="/apps/">All apps</a></p>
</div></section>

<section id="sync" class="chapter" data-scene="sync" aria-label="Sync"><div class="chapter__inner">
<h2>Every device keeps the whole collection</h2>
<p>With the desktop app, your computers keep a complete copy of the collection as ordinary files. Each copy works offline and catches up when it reconnects.</p>
<p>When the same record is edited in two places, mdbase works out what each edit changed, field by field, and combines edits to different fields.</p>
<p>Changes are encrypted and signed on the device that made them before they are sent.</p>
</div></section>

<section id="anywhere" class="chapter" data-scene="serve" aria-label="Apps on any device"><div class="chapter__inner">
<h2>Open it from any device</h2>
<p>mdbase also keeps a copy of the collection and serves it to your apps. TaskNotes on your phone or the Editor in a browser opens the collection through mdbase, and keeps working while your computers are switched off.</p>
<p>A new device joins when you sign in. A new account starts with a small collection that opens in the Editor straight away, before you install anything.</p>
<p>The <a href="/security/">security page</a> sets out what mdbase stores and can read, and the option to sync a collection that mdbase can’t read.</p>
</div></section>

<section id="permission" class="chapter" data-scene="grant" aria-label="Application access"><div class="chapter__inner">
<h2>Apps ask first</h2>
<p>An app asks for access to one collection and lists the operations it needs. You might let a project planner find, create and edit project records while leaving deletion blocked.</p>
<p>You approve each app in Connect, and you can narrow or revoke its access at any time. Revoking it ends the app’s sessions.</p>
</div></section>

<section id="sharing" class="chapter" data-scene="sharing" aria-label="Sharing"><div class="chapter__inner">
<h2>Share a collection</h2>
<p>Invite viewers, who can read, or editors, who can also change records. Each person uses their own apps, within the role you gave them.</p>
<p>You can change a member’s role or remove them at any time. A removed member stops receiving changes and keeps the files they already had.</p>
</div></section>

<section id="start" class="chapter" data-scene="intro" aria-label="Get started"><div class="chapter__inner">
<h2>Get started</h2>
<p>Create an account to open your first collection in the Editor. To sync a folder on your computer, install the desktop app. Apps receive no access until you approve them.</p>
<div class="chapter__actions home-actions"><a class="home-action home-action--primary" href="https://connect.mdbase.dev/signup">Create an account</a><a class="home-action" href="/downloads/">Download the desktop app</a></div>
<dl class="v2-facts">
<div><dt>Status</dt><dd>Connect is in beta and has no availability guarantee. Service incidents are summarised on the <a href="/incidents/">incidents page</a>.</dd></div>
<div><dt>Source</dt><dd>The specification, Connect, Reader and Writer are open source under the MIT licence, <a href="https://github.com/mdbase-dev">on GitHub</a>.</dd></div>
<div><dt>Developers</dt><dd>Any app can work with a collection. Read the <a href="/sdk/">SDK documentation</a> and the <a href="/spec/">specification</a>.</dd></div>
</dl>
</div></section>
</main>
</HomeLayout>
